# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Model artefacts — both files are committed, because they are small and
# because tools/selftest.py needs model.pt to prove the numpy inference
# matches the PyTorch model it was exported from.
#   runs/weights.npz   47 KB — what the deployed app loads
#   runs/model.pt      26 KB — the torch checkpoint, for training and the
#                        numpy-vs-torch equivalence check
#
# The evaluation output is committed too. It used to be ignored as
# "scratch", which was a mistake: the README states that every figure in
# §5 comes from runs/eval/metrics.json, so a reviewer who cannot reach
# that file cannot check the claim. It is 57 KB in total.
#
#   runs/eval/metrics.json    — the held-out evaluation (200 scenes)
#   runs/eval/confusion.png   — the normalised confusion matrix
#   runs/eval/report.md       — the same table in markdown
#
# Only the training scratch logs are ignored.
runs/train_log.txt

